# Acuitas — build settings
#
# Copy this file to .env.production, fill in the values, then run
#   npm ci && npm run build
# Vite reads .env.production automatically for `npm run build`.
# .env.production is git-ignored: it never goes into the repository.
#
# Leave everything blank to build the self-contained demonstration copy
# (local mode: data stays in each browser, nothing is shared or sent).

# ── Where the app lives ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# URL path the app is served from. "/" for its own hostname
# (https://acuitas.example.org/), or "/acuitas/" for a sub-path.
ACUITAS_BASE=/
# Folder the build is written to. "dist" for a standalone repository.
ACUITAS_OUT_DIR=dist

# ── Shared database: the Acuitas data service (recommended) ─────────
# Shared data in your organization's SQL Server, Azure SQL or PostgreSQL,
# through the data service in api/ (see api/README.md). Requires sign-in
# through your single sign-on (gateway, below).
# VITE_BACKEND=api
# Where the data service answers, relative to the site. Default /api.
# VITE_API_BASE=/api
# How often (milliseconds) each screen checks for other people's changes.
# Default 4000.
# VITE_API_POLL_MS=4000

# ── Sign-in ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# local    = no SSO; names are self-entered (demo / training only)
# gateway  = SSO enforced in front of the app (Azure Static Web Apps with
#            Microsoft Entra ID, or a sign-in proxy). REQUIRED with the data
#            service above.
# firebase = Firebase Authentication (reference option only, below)
# VITE_AUTH_MODE=gateway

# Gateway mode:
# VITE_IDENTITY_ENDPOINT=/.auth/me
# VITE_SIGN_IN_URL=/.auth/login/aad
# With Azure Static Web Apps, leave VITE_ROLE_MAP blank: the data service maps
# Entra ID groups to roles at sign-in (ACUITAS_ROLE_MAP, api/README.md).
# Behind another sign-in proxy, map your directory groups here, and set the
# same map as ACUITAS_ROLE_MAP on the data service:
# VITE_ROLE_MAP={"BH-House-Supervisors":"supervisor","BH-Charge-RNs":"charge"}

# ── Reference only: Google Cloud Firestore ──────────────────────────
# Not for organizations that do not permit Google Cloud. Building this option
# needs the Firebase library first:  npm install firebase@^12.14.0
# VITE_FIREBASE_CONFIG={"apiKey":"...","authDomain":"...","projectId":"...","storageBucket":"...","messagingSenderId":"...","appId":"..."}
# VITE_AUTH_MODE=firebase
# VITE_AUTH_PROVIDER_ID=oidc.entra
